# Store everything as LF in git, regardless of what the working copy uses.
# Windows checkouts still get CRLF locally; this just stops the repo itself from
# holding mixed line endings, which is what produces the "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warning on every commit from this machine and shows spurious whole-file
# diffs when the site is cloned on macOS or Linux (or built on Netlify).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — git must never try to normalise these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
